WEBVTT

00:11.000 --> 00:15.390
Daa! Daa! Daa!

00:11.310 --> 00:15.180
The moment we sat facing each other

00:11.310 --> 00:15.180
Mukai awase ni suwatta shunkan ni

00:15.650 --> 00:19.970
my heart was thumping at the sideways view of your adult-like face

00:15.650 --> 00:19.970
otona no yokogao ni DOKI DOKI shiteru no

00:20.320 --> 00:24.060
Although you're always beside me

00:20.320 --> 00:24.060
Itsudemo soba ni iru hazu demo

00:24.360 --> 00:28.730
the truth is I don't really know much about you

00:24.360 --> 00:28.730
hontou wa KIMI no koto yoku shiranai yo ne

00:28.910 --> 00:37.450
We're always playing with our friends

00:28.910 --> 00:37.450
Itsumo nakamatachi to asonderu kedo

00:37.630 --> 00:43.290
but when we're alone, something's different

00:37.630 --> 00:43.290
futarikiri ni naru to doko ka chigau yo

00:43.880 --> 00:46.830
Talk to me about something

00:43.880 --> 00:46.830
Nanika hanashi kakete

00:47.550 --> 00:51.960
I've always loved you more than anyone else

00:47.550 --> 00:51.960
Zutto dare yori mo daisuki da yo

00:52.020 --> 00:56.300
but I can't say it, you're too close

00:52.020 --> 00:56.300
dakedo ienai yo chikasugiru yo

00:56.440 --> 01:00.430
Someday, notice I'm gazing at you

00:56.440 --> 01:00.430
Itsuka kizuite yo mitsumeteru yo

01:00.440 --> 01:04.890
When we plant the seeds of love

01:00.440 --> 01:04.890
Koi no TANE wo maitara

01:05.030 --> 01:09.150
see, they will all bloom fully

01:05.030 --> 01:09.150
hora sakasou yo ippai

01:09.530 --> 01:14.950
That's my wish to God

01:09.530 --> 01:14.950
Mou kamisama ni onegai

01:20.480 --> 01:22.390
The massive space time distortion ….

01:25.800 --> 01:29.460
It looks like the rescue ship is stuck in the warp.

01:29.460 --> 01:30.810
In such a situation,

01:30.810 --> 01:34.240
if the distortion were to weaken, it’d be great, but…

01:34.240 --> 01:36.170
Don't tell me...

01:36.820 --> 01:41.080
Let’s Meet Again

01:44.480 --> 01:48.420
Wh-wh-what’s that!!? It’s scary!!

01:53.880 --> 01:55.480
Ah…that’s….

01:55.480 --> 01:56.490
Is that...?

01:56.490 --> 01:58.340
We’ve seen it before.

02:01.500 --> 02:03.470
Peace to the Earth

02:03.470 --> 02:04.760
It's the Waru-waru guys!!

02:04.760 --> 02:05.600
That’s right.

02:05.600 --> 02:07.130
It’s that wicked lady.

02:08.860 --> 02:11.650
Oh! It’s Guava-san and her sisters.

02:11.650 --> 02:14.610
There was nothing to get scared about.

02:15.260 --> 02:18.250
Really? You and Guava-chan are aliens too?

02:18.250 --> 02:19.080
Yep…

02:19.080 --> 02:20.820
We are from the planet Sharaku.

02:21.120 --> 02:24.850
I didn’t know that Guava-san was an alien.

02:24.850 --> 02:26.790
Do-do you hate me?

02:27.370 --> 02:29.500
Of course not.

02:29.500 --> 02:31.660
Whether you’re an alien or from Earth,

02:31.660 --> 02:35.940
it doesn’t change the fact that you’re a wonderful girl.

02:36.430 --> 02:37.220
Hikarigaoka-san…

02:37.570 --> 02:39.380
This is wonderful! Super wonderful!

02:39.380 --> 02:42.850
I didn’t know that there are girls who are aliens!

02:42.850 --> 02:45.560
I get it! That person’s also the same, isn’t she?

02:45.560 --> 02:46.890
That person?

02:46.890 --> 02:47.940
Mikan-san.

02:47.940 --> 02:49.010
Nope.

02:49.010 --> 02:50.870
She’s just an ordinary shoujo manga artist.

02:50.870 --> 02:53.400
She’s an authentic human being.

02:53.400 --> 02:54.530
You lie!

02:54.530 --> 02:55.750
It’s true.

02:57.690 --> 03:04.060
I see. So human beings who are terrible are like aliens. It makes sense.

03:04.380 --> 03:06.290
It doesn’t make any sense.

03:06.290 --> 03:11.500
Waru-waru guys! Sorry if you’ve dropped in to visit, but we’re in the middle of something important.

03:11.800 --> 03:14.840
The rescue ship is caught in the space-time distortion, right?

03:14.840 --> 03:16.510
Huh? How do you-?

03:16.510 --> 03:19.750
We’re here to do something about it.

03:19.750 --> 03:20.730
What do you mean?

03:20.730 --> 03:22.190
What the heck do you mean?

03:23.360 --> 03:24.910
You asked me, right?

03:24.910 --> 03:27.350
You asked little ol’ me, right?

03:27.350 --> 03:29.520
Let’s show them!
-Okay

03:30.560 --> 03:36.230
That’s right, ladies and gentlemen, the product we’re going to show you today

03:36.230 --> 03:39.230
the device that will control and stop the space-time distortion,
Tomechau-kun.

03:39.230 --> 03:42.740
It’s a new product, so we won’t be putting it up for sale today.

03:42.740 --> 03:44.600
A device…

03:44.600 --> 03:46.700
To control the space-time distortion…

03:48.130 --> 03:50.780
The invention you were working on before is complete?

03:50.780 --> 03:52.710
It’s a new product.

03:52.710 --> 03:58.300
The umbrella on top of Tomechau-kun’s head can be unfurled to fix the space time distortion.

03:58.300 --> 04:02.260
While that’s happening, the rescue ship from Otto will be freed.

03:58.300 --> 04:02.260
Rescue ship

03:58.300 --> 04:02.260
Earth

04:02.300 --> 04:03.870
Is it really possible?

04:03.870 --> 04:05.340
Trust me!

04:05.340 --> 04:07.650
Can we really do it, Waru-waru-kun?

04:07.650 --> 04:08.350
But…

04:08.350 --> 04:12.600
The force that’s sucked in the rescue ship is so strong,

04:12.640 --> 04:17.900
there’s the possibility that the instant our ship nears it, it’ll also be sucked in.

04:18.760 --> 04:20.110
But that’s okay.

04:20.110 --> 04:23.150
Durian has an idea.

04:24.320 --> 04:27.450
We will need to power up our ship.

04:28.170 --> 04:32.960
I see. So if we link Waru-waru’s space craft with ours-

04:32.960 --> 04:35.830
We’ll be able to get four times the power,right?

04:35.830 --> 04:37.100
That’s right.

04:37.100 --> 04:38.790
How is that going to help the rescue ship?

04:38.790 --> 04:40.300
We’ll be able to save it.

04:41.960 --> 04:46.380
Oh! It's brilliant, absolutely brilliant!

04:46.380 --> 04:51.890
You will have four times the power! Now I get it!

04:52.150 --> 04:54.680
I’m so glad! I’m so glad!

04:54.680 --> 04:57.060
It’s great, isn’t it, Ruu?

04:58.850 --> 05:02.900
Durian-san, Kiwi-san, Guava-chan, thank you!

05:02.900 --> 05:07.960
What are you saying? We’ve given you guys so much trouble.

05:07.960 --> 05:08.860
Yes

05:08.860 --> 05:13.330
So we, the Waru Waru gang, have now turned into good guys.

05:14.010 --> 05:16.010
Look! We’ve changed, haven’t we?

05:16.010 --> 05:17.460
Yes, you’ve changed!

05:17.460 --> 05:21.420
Okay! Then let’s hurry up with the space ship linking.

05:21.420 --> 05:25.790
Yes, before the rescue ship gets sucked in any further.

05:25.790 --> 05:27.810
Let’s do it right away!

05:27.810 --> 05:30.110
Of course we’ll also help out.

05:30.110 --> 05:33.760
Even though we know nothing about aliens

05:33.760 --> 05:36.110
But there must be something we can do.

05:36.110 --> 05:37.520
We’ll do anything.

05:37.520 --> 05:38.940
You guys…

05:38.940 --> 05:41.290
Of course I will also help out too.

05:41.290 --> 05:43.030
Count me in!

05:43.430 --> 05:47.790
It’s for Miyu-chi and my rival Saionji-kun, after all!

05:47.790 --> 05:49.370
I’m not your rival.

05:49.370 --> 05:52.800
You guys! This is friendship! This is the springtime of life!

05:52.800 --> 05:55.690
The Waru-waru gang are your friends now, right?

05:55.690 --> 05:59.790
You guys, let’s prepare ourselves!

06:00.250 --> 06:05.220
We will show these aliens just what
we can do here at Izumo temple!

06:05.220 --> 06:06.130
Isn’t that great!

06:06.130 --> 06:08.280
Thank you, everyone.

06:08.280 --> 06:09.450
Thank you

06:12.450 --> 06:14.310
Let’s do our best!

06:14.520 --> 06:17.610
Kanata-kun, I'll leave everything here to you.

06:17.610 --> 06:18.440
O-ok

06:18.440 --> 06:23.250
Let’s inform the Space Police Force and check on the state of the space time distortion.

06:23.250 --> 06:25.390
Alright! Leave that to me!

06:25.390 --> 06:28.060
Let’s first split up collect the important material.

06:28.060 --> 06:29.200
Yeah!!

06:29.200 --> 06:30.620
Supermarket
Mega bargain sale

06:35.300 --> 06:38.000
Wow! So many things we can use…

06:38.000 --> 06:42.360
We can use all of this to make our invention the best!

06:42.360 --> 06:45.920
No…no. Far from being of use,
this is just stuff that was thrown away.

06:47.920 --> 06:49.790
You’re doing great, Santa-kun!

06:49.790 --> 06:52.890
I've always been good at building things, and this is fun.

06:52.910 --> 06:54.980
I see.

06:54.980 --> 06:59.390
I’m so happy I could be of help to Kanata-kun.

06:59.390 --> 07:02.360
“Ah, Chris, I know I haven’t said it till now,

07:02.360 --> 07:06.480
but a girl who can make beautiful wood shavings is just my type.”

07:06.480 --> 07:09.230
“Really? Kanata-kun…”

07:09.230 --> 07:12.820
“Damn straight! You’re my ideal girl.”

07:12.820 --> 07:14.040
Wheee!!!

07:14.620 --> 07:16.580
Chris-chan’s full of determination.

07:16.580 --> 07:19.980
I want to make the space belt for Tomechau-kun but…

07:19.980 --> 07:24.240
Leave it to me. I’ve been hanging out with Aya long enough to know how to get outfits done.

07:24.240 --> 07:26.300
Easy-peasy!

07:27.850 --> 07:33.460
This space-time distortion is really terrible. But I won’t give up!

07:33.460 --> 07:36.180
Yosh! I wonder how the rest of them are faring out there.

07:36.180 --> 07:37.990
Hey! Guys!

07:38.270 --> 07:41.250
I’m sorry! It was an accident!

07:41.250 --> 07:45.390
Hey, if you’re going to get in the way of others, just do your work over there.

07:45.390 --> 07:46.480
O…kay...

07:50.530 --> 07:54.960
I wonder where I can get something that’s light and two centimetres long…

07:56.230 --> 07:59.080
I’m sorry, Okame-chan. We’re doing it for Ruu-kun.

08:01.260 --> 08:02.670
Will this do?

08:02.670 --> 08:09.160
Thank you. I also need something that’s 6 cm long,  straight and swishy…

08:10.810 --> 08:14.680
I get it, Okame-chan. We’re doing it for Ruu-kun…

08:16.120 --> 08:18.000
Thank you, you two!

08:19.790 --> 08:23.750
I want three wheels that are of the same dimension…

08:23.750 --> 08:25.310
How about this?

08:28.320 --> 08:30.530
But…isn’t that your most important-

08:30.530 --> 08:32.800
It’s for my beloved Ruu.

08:33.620 --> 08:34.660
Momoko-chan…

08:35.340 --> 08:36.120
Momo!

08:36.500 --> 08:38.160
Ruu!

08:43.650 --> 08:48.700
The perfect snack for an all-nighter.
The special Sharaku-don gives stamina.

08:48.700 --> 08:52.170
I hope this is all right with the aliens.

08:52.170 --> 08:53.370
I hope so.

08:53.370 --> 08:55.470
Miyu! It’s time!

08:55.850 --> 08:56.870
Time…?

08:56.870 --> 09:00.430
What are you saying? It’s time for the launch of the space shuttle!

09:00.430 --> 09:02.150
What? Already?

09:02.150 --> 09:05.730
Don’t say that so casually! It’s being broadcast on TV right now.

09:06.510 --> 09:12.920
Here they come! They’ll be boarding the shuttle soon. I can see Kozuki Miki-san.

09:12.920 --> 09:13.860
Mom…

09:17.090 --> 09:18.910
The time has finally come.

09:18.910 --> 09:20.060
Miki!

09:20.060 --> 09:20.580
Huh?

09:20.580 --> 09:23.000
Good luck, Miki!

09:31.090 --> 09:34.840
I’m going to fulfill my dream. Darling….Miyu…

09:35.230 --> 09:36.430
Have a safe trip…

09:50.140 --> 09:53.360
They’re ascending! Look at them go!

09:55.390 --> 09:57.280
Congratulations, Mom!

09:57.710 --> 10:02.690
Guys, let’s celebrate the huge success of the launch with a special Sharaku-don!

10:02.690 --> 10:03.740
Yeah!

10:09.230 --> 10:10.960
Okay! It’s done!

10:18.030 --> 10:20.970
With this the rescue ship can be saved, right?

10:20.970 --> 10:24.670
Yeah. We made it perfect.

10:25.430 --> 10:27.400
It’s great, isn’t it, Ruu-kun?

10:28.480 --> 10:31.100
Oh no!

10:31.100 --> 10:33.650
The distortion has reached epic proportions!

10:34.410 --> 10:39.200
It’s spread out and is taking over the entire earth!

10:51.080 --> 10:53.040
It’s taking over the entire earth!

10:53.340 --> 10:55.620
The earth’s not visible!

10:55.620 --> 10:57.890
This is the first time I’m seeing something like this.

10:57.890 --> 11:00.430
What-what about Mom’s shuttle?

11:00.430 --> 11:07.180
Don’t worry. Luckily, the shuttle is in a different orbit than this. So it’s not affected.

11:07.180 --> 11:08.810
I see. Thank God!

11:08.810 --> 11:10.730
Oh no!!

11:11.560 --> 11:16.620
In such a situation there won’t be enough power to use Tomechau-kun’s umbrella!

11:16.620 --> 11:17.990
What does that mean?

11:17.990 --> 11:23.320
We need the power of one umbrella cassette in order to resist the space time warp.

11:24.140 --> 11:26.330
If the warp is taking over the whole area,

11:26.330 --> 11:29.750
then we have to use an umbrella cassette to get out.

11:29.750 --> 11:33.540
We need one more to get the rescue ship out as well.

11:33.540 --> 11:36.390
But we have only these two!

11:36.390 --> 11:39.510
In other words, we don’t have enough cassettes to get back to Saionji.

11:40.730 --> 11:41.900
No way!

11:41.900 --> 11:44.750
You mean you can’t get that kind of power on earth?

11:44.750 --> 11:45.710
Not on Earth.

11:45.710 --> 11:46.750
Only two cassettes!

11:46.750 --> 11:47.700
Only these two.

11:47.700 --> 11:48.930
One was for coming back.

11:49.310 --> 11:51.360
What should we do?

11:52.640 --> 11:54.900
There’s a way.

11:55.950 --> 11:57.180
A way?

11:57.180 --> 12:01.230
Ruu and the others should get onto this space ship along with his UFO.

12:01.230 --> 12:01.810
Huh?

12:01.810 --> 12:05.320
Once the Otto ship is rescued from the warp, instead of returning to Earth,

12:05.320 --> 12:10.630
Ruu and the others should be sent there in the UFO.

12:10.630 --> 12:12.160
Oh! I see…

12:12.160 --> 12:13.450
Papa…

12:13.450 --> 12:14.040
But…

12:14.040 --> 12:18.650
That means we have to part with Ruu-kun and the others right here and now.

12:18.650 --> 12:19.340
Ruu…

12:19.340 --> 12:20.260
Miyu-cchi…

12:28.050 --> 12:37.270
If Ruu-kun is able to return to his parents, it’s ok if we have to part here. Right, Kanata?

12:37.660 --> 12:38.590
Miyu…

12:42.070 --> 12:44.410
mama…papa…

12:45.050 --> 12:45.980
Ruu-kun

13:02.740 --> 13:07.930
I thought we’d have more time, so I didn’t think to prepare myself.

13:07.930 --> 13:10.310
Yeah, you’re right.

13:11.240 --> 13:16.450
Kanata-san…Miyu-san….thank you for everything.

13:16.450 --> 13:20.650
I don’t know what would have happened to us if we hadn’t met you both.

13:20.650 --> 13:23.810
No…I should be saying that.

13:23.810 --> 13:24.910
Me too.

13:30.690 --> 13:35.540
Otto may be far off but we’ll be able to meet again, won’t we?

13:36.790 --> 13:37.710
Yeah

13:41.680 --> 13:45.940
I know! Next time we meet, we’ll dig up the time capsules that we buried!

13:45.940 --> 13:53.150
That’s right. Let’s hurry up...with everyone….

13:55.500 --> 13:57.600
I’m crying…

13:59.320 --> 14:00.690
Wannya…

14:01.100 --> 14:04.830
Mama…papa…

14:05.470 --> 14:06.690
Ruu-kun…

14:06.690 --> 14:08.030
Wannya…

14:11.710 --> 14:13.120
Ruu-chama…

14:17.090 --> 14:17.830
Ruu-kun!

14:18.980 --> 14:20.440
Ruu-chama!

14:31.350 --> 14:34.850
This is Ruu’s toy. I shrunk it with the mini-mini machine.

14:34.850 --> 14:37.820
It’s also got Kabokichi-san’s melon inside it.

14:38.570 --> 14:42.500
This is the photo that we took in Momonland. Please treasure it.

14:42.500 --> 14:44.160
Yes, Momo

14:45.980 --> 14:48.030
Ruu….

14:48.030 --> 14:50.210
Here are some dumplings.

14:50.210 --> 14:52.270
The recipe is also included.

14:52.270 --> 14:54.160
Thank you

14:54.160 --> 14:57.620
Here’s a record that I would like you to play for Ruu-kun.

14:57.620 --> 14:59.320
Thank you, Santa-san.

14:59.320 --> 15:01.590
Some rice balls for Pepo.

15:01.590 --> 15:02.710
Pepo Pepo

15:02.710 --> 15:05.170
I’m giving you roses that grow on Earth.

15:05.860 --> 15:07.770
Adios, Guava-cchi.

15:07.770 --> 15:09.380
Thank you, my Prince.

15:09.380 --> 15:11.800
Alright! We’re leaving now.

15:12.110 --> 15:15.040
Please take care of Ruu and the others.

15:15.040 --> 15:16.270
Please…

15:16.530 --> 15:17.760
Leave it to us.

15:17.760 --> 15:18.970
Don’t worry.

15:18.970 --> 15:20.210
Take care, Wannya.

15:20.210 --> 15:23.390
Yes. Well, then, Ruu-chama, shall we go?

15:25.290 --> 15:29.630
No! Mama! Papa!

15:29.630 --> 15:30.400
Ruu-chama…

15:31.850 --> 15:32.570
Ruu-kun…

15:32.920 --> 15:35.370
Mama! Papa!

15:40.110 --> 15:40.980
Miyu…

15:41.530 --> 15:46.340
It’s alright…it’s alright…I’m ok…I’m ok…

15:46.340 --> 15:48.930
I’m also ok.

15:51.320 --> 15:52.210
Ruu…

15:52.560 --> 15:53.300
Ruu-kun…

15:55.590 --> 15:57.710
Ruu, see you.

15:57.710 --> 15:59.730
Have a safe trip, Ruu-kun.

16:00.240 --> 16:02.690
Mama…Papa…

16:05.130 --> 16:08.230
Miyu-san, Kanata-san…We're going now.

16:08.230 --> 16:12.780
Have a safe trip…see you…

16:21.910 --> 16:22.790
Take off!

16:34.430 --> 16:35.410
Ruu!

16:35.410 --> 16:36.550
Ruu-kun!

16:51.900 --> 16:55.860
Space-time Distortion Control Device Tomechau-kun Cassette….on!

16:56.140 --> 16:56.960
On!

17:06.540 --> 17:07.500
Lets go!

17:07.500 --> 17:08.560
Wow!

17:08.560 --> 17:10.390
Just what I expected from you, Waru-waru-kun!

17:10.390 --> 17:11.550
We’re the good guys now.

17:18.010 --> 17:20.680
Detecting the rescue ship from Otto

17:24.950 --> 17:26.780
Papa…Mama…

17:26.780 --> 17:30.610
That’s right, Ruu-chama. Papa and Mama are inside that.

17:30.610 --> 17:31.950
Advance at Full Speed!

17:31.950 --> 17:33.110
Advancing at Full Speed!

17:39.260 --> 17:40.740
We’re being pulled in!

17:42.200 --> 17:44.700
Insert the next cassette into Tomechau-kun!

17:44.700 --> 17:46.160
Cassette On!

17:47.830 --> 17:49.960
This is a stronger cassette that the one before!

18:01.050 --> 18:02.960
All right!

18:04.040 --> 18:06.570
It’s alright now, Ruu-chama!

18:07.460 --> 18:10.830
We’re proceeding towards the rescue ship now.

18:10.830 --> 18:11.950
Okay.

18:13.760 --> 18:15.610
What’s the matter, Tomecha-kun?

18:15.610 --> 18:18.570
Oh no! The time-warp is closing in!

18:19.390 --> 18:20.990
I guess that’s it.

18:21.580 --> 18:22.960
No way!

18:22.960 --> 18:23.990
To have come so far and now….

18:24.710 --> 18:26.870
Wannya, you and Ruu-kun will take off in Ruu-kun’s UFO!

18:27.620 --> 18:31.380
If you go now you can make it!

18:31.380 --> 18:34.170
B-but, just the two of us-

18:34.170 --> 18:35.570
You’ll be fine, so hurry up!

18:35.570 --> 18:41.230
We’re genius scientists. We’ll power up Tomechau-kun and then get out of here.

18:41.230 --> 18:41.850
But-

18:41.850 --> 18:44.560
Wannya, you’re a sitter-pet.

18:44.560 --> 18:47.060
And being a sitter-pet means,

18:47.060 --> 18:49.850
your number one priority is to protect the baby at all times!

18:51.300 --> 18:52.430
Wannya

18:53.220 --> 18:54.400
Ruu-chama…

18:55.530 --> 18:56.960
That’s right.

18:56.960 --> 19:03.060
I could not protect Ruu-chama when the distortion brought us here from Otto.

19:03.060 --> 19:05.750
But this time, this time I’ll definitely

19:05.750 --> 19:09.710
take Ruu-chama to the rescue ship. It's my duty!

19:09.710 --> 19:10.540
Wannya!

19:11.550 --> 19:16.630
Please leave it to this pet from Otto.

19:20.130 --> 19:21.340
Ready?

19:21.340 --> 19:22.470
Yes, please.

19:22.470 --> 19:26.240
Ruu-kun, you’re going to be totally spoiled by your parents!

19:26.240 --> 19:27.470
Launch.

19:32.410 --> 19:37.030
Miyu-san, Kanata-san, I’ll take care of Ruu-chama.

19:38.990 --> 19:40.080
Wannya!

19:40.080 --> 19:42.170
It’s going to be alright, Ruu-chama.

19:42.170 --> 19:42.990
Pepo

19:52.140 --> 19:54.620
Hurry up and power up, Waru-waru-kun!

19:54.620 --> 19:56.640
We’re the good guys! Get out of the way!

19:56.340 --> 20:06.050
Supermarket

19:57.050 --> 20:00.600
That's it! The supermarket is the most super!

20:00.600 --> 20:03.100
We’re not at all worried about the warp.

20:03.100 --> 20:06.050
You can take us there. It’s the supermarket, after all.

20:06.050 --> 20:08.470
What! Is that how you power up!?

20:08.470 --> 20:11.870
This time there’s no other way but to do this.

20:16.830 --> 20:18.230
What did you do?

20:18.230 --> 20:19.210
Oops!

20:19.210 --> 20:21.390
Oh no! We’re done for!

20:24.810 --> 20:30.930
Farewell…..!

20:34.340 --> 20:36.670
How does it feel to be have your dream come true?

20:36.670 --> 20:41.090
Wonderful! I’m in space right now.

20:42.190 --> 20:46.590
Huh? A UFO?

20:50.490 --> 20:52.520
A…liens…?

21:11.180 --> 21:13.330
Your mother called from NASA?

21:13.330 --> 21:16.340
Yeah. She said she saw it from the shuttle.

21:16.340 --> 21:20.590
A baby in a UFO getting into a huge space ship.

21:20.590 --> 21:24.730
It was accompanied by a creature that looked like a dog or a cat.

21:24.730 --> 21:25.760
That’s got to be Wannya.

21:26.070 --> 21:28.190
Miyu’s mother was very excited.

21:28.190 --> 21:32.850
Her dream of going to space was fulfilled and she got to see an alien.

21:32.850 --> 21:33.930
Really?

21:33.930 --> 21:38.270
Ruu-kun, you’ve re-united with your mom and dad safe and sound…

21:38.270 --> 21:40.390
I’m glad!

21:40.860 --> 21:45.530
But…it’s kind of lonely without them, isn’t it?

21:46.160 --> 21:47.530
Yeah…

21:49.630 --> 21:52.220
It’s lonely… but not really.

21:52.220 --> 21:53.040
That’s right.

21:53.340 --> 21:54.270
Huh?

21:54.730 --> 21:59.910
I mean, they are just right on the other side of this sky on Otto.

21:59.910 --> 22:02.960
He must be enjoying himself with his family.

22:02.960 --> 22:06.470
We also had fun when they were here.

22:06.470 --> 22:08.050
Yeah, it was fun.

22:08.350 --> 22:09.420
You’re right.

22:09.420 --> 22:10.520
That’s right.

22:10.520 --> 22:11.340
Yeah.

22:11.340 --> 22:12.630
We had fun.

22:12.630 --> 22:14.240
We had fun.

22:23.200 --> 22:28.020
I felt that everyday

22:23.200 --> 22:28.020
Motto tanoshii koto ga

22:28.660 --> 22:31.650
more fun-filled days

22:28.660 --> 22:31.650
afureru mainichi

22:32.450 --> 22:36.780
were waiting ahead

22:32.450 --> 22:36.780
matteru kigashita

22:38.630 --> 22:46.130
because I was able to meet you again

22:38.630 --> 22:46.130
datte kimi to mata aeta kara

22:46.220 --> 22:51.950
Hey, don't be in rush now

22:46.220 --> 22:51.950
Nee ima wa aserazu

22:53.140 --> 22:56.510
Walk slowly

22:53.140 --> 22:56.510
Yukkuri aruite

22:56.810 --> 23:00.300
Laugh a lot

22:56.810 --> 23:00.300
Takusan waratte

23:00.570 --> 23:04.640
And when you find something

23:00.570 --> 23:04.640
Soshite nanika wo mitsuketara

23:04.870 --> 23:08.230
let's cherish it

23:04.870 --> 23:08.230
daiji ni shiyou

23:08.700 --> 23:11.900
until we meet again

23:08.700 --> 23:11.900
mata aeta ne

23:12.450 --> 23:17.950
Let's stay together

23:12.450 --> 23:17.950
Issho ni iyou

23:17.950 --> 23:21.950
Special thanks to Aozora-subs: Ruu-chan and Redbird-chan TL/Edit
Tmusubs: Onidragon-kun Tl/Edit/Time, Creative TLC, All the mistakes...

23:33.430 --> 23:34.890
Hello, Miyu-san.

23:35.720 --> 23:37.760
Come in, Momoko-chan.

23:37.760 --> 23:39.060
Kanata-san!

23:40.000 --> 23:40.480
Hey!

23:40.790 --> 23:42.060
You’re on your way back from school?

23:42.060 --> 23:44.650
Yeah. Just wanted to show my face.

23:44.650 --> 23:46.670
Hello, Miu-chan!

23:46.670 --> 23:48.190
Momo.

23:50.930 --> 23:55.910
I see. You’re just like how Ruu-kun used to be.

24:00.580 --> 24:02.460
Pepo! Pepo! Pepo!

24:05.270 --> 24:06.030
Pepo?

24:06.030 --> 24:07.210
Pepo?

24:09.470 --> 24:10.170
Pepo!

24:10.170 --> 24:11.920
Is it really Pepo?

24:11.920 --> 24:12.810
Pepo!

24:26.670 --> 24:27.730
Wannya!

24:29.850 --> 24:30.940
Wannya!

24:36.260 --> 24:37.370
Ruu…

24:37.840 --> 24:38.660
Ruu…

24:39.710 --> 24:42.050
Ruu-kun…

24:46.290 --> 24:47.390
I’m home!

24:48.770 --> 24:49.920
Welcome back!

24:53.170 --> 24:58.870
They could meet again
